Target flags: $(<name>.import.target target,program,flags) and its star form
$(<name>.import.target* var,flags) take the engine's flags for the target, so an at line
above a define passes them as @jq.import.target --null-input. The target records the
flags, a kept value's reader copies them, and the job puts them ahead of the program on
the engine's command line. jq no longer gets -n behind the user's back: a jq target reads
its standard input as any jq does, and one that generates its value without input says
--null-input. The star form dereferences only the variable, so the flags pass as written.

